                                        "entry_id": "a7025342-c11c-3f73-bb47-d739e4c9f616",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who or that which corrupts."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4459b4e6-484d-4cf8-ab54-03d6225aaa2e",
                                                "sense_id": "4fb8e4d5-9c87-3126-911d-9b4ce5e3aacc",
                                                "text": "Can love, which always seeks the good of its object, attempt to betray a woman into a bargain where she is so greatly to be the loser? If such corrupter, therefore, should have the impudence to pretend a real affection for her, ought not the woman to regard him […] as the worst of all enemies […] ?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "68836ebc-649a-43af-9caa-55f6c215c673",
                                                "sense_id": "4fb8e4d5-9c87-3126-911d-9b4ce5e3aacc",
                                                "text": "Since the 1980s, video games have widely been lambasted as a medium that is at best a waste of time and at worst a training ground for violence and aggression. Despite popularized media depictions of video games as corrupters of youth, to date, no study has definitively demonstrated any such link […]"
                                            }
